    NPC: It's quiet at the cache spot. Esperanza doesn't say much. Sometimes that's the whole point.
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Like I said — We were just talking. Nothing important."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "We're going in circles a bit — Small talk, that's all. Nothing worth repeating. Ask me something else if you want."
    YOU: "Want to come with us?"
    NPC: "Yes. Absolutely. I've been hoping you'd ask." (A little too quickly.)
    YOU: "Can I ask you something else?"
    NPC: "Right — go on, I'm listening."
    YOU: "I owe you. Let me make it right — what do you need?"
    NPC: "Okay. Here’s the thing —"
    YOU: "We're square."
    NPC: "Well." A breath. "That's where things stand."
    YOU: "Don't mention it."
    NPC: "So." They look at the fire for a moment.
    YOU: "Don't mention it."
    NPC: "Anyway." A small smile.
    YOU: "We're square."
    NPC: They nod slowly, not quite done, not quite continuing.
    NPC: "Okay. We'll pick this up later."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: A comfortable quiet settles. They smile a little, and let it be.
    NPC: "Good — that debt, settled. Feels better said out loud."
    NPC: "This was good." They mean it.

